 "transcript": {
  "answer": "Petrol is about **13.5% dearer than a year ago**. The latest ABS figure is for **August 2026**, when the automotive fuel price index was 112.95, against 99.49 in August 2025.\n\nThe index covers all automotive fuel, not just unleaded, and it measures percentage change rather than cents per litre, so I can't give you an exact dollar figure per litre from this data.\n\nPrices have been volatile this year. Fuel jumped 24.2% year-on-year in March 2026 and 18.6% in April, then fell 7.3% in June before rising again. The August rise was a sharp 13.5% from July's 98.4 index level.",
